If a patient has a serious-illness and has a poor-return-to-previous-function-prognosis then it is possible that an opioid possibly is an appropriate-therapy for the patient.
If a patient has an alternative-therapy-contraindication then it is possible that an opioid possibly is an appropriate-therapy for the patient.
If a clinician has an overriding-patient-comfort-goal-agreement with a patient then it is possible that an opioid possibly is an appropriate-therapy for the patient.
